From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: no webview is given a page Chrome serves itself

chrome:// and chrome-untrusted:// are Chrome's UI for Chrome's window, and
a desk has none. Worse, they assume one: HistoryUI looks its tab up
unconditionally, so chrome://history opened in a <webview>, whose guest
is in no tab strip, took the browser process down in
TabInterface::GetFromContents.

CreateAndAddChromeThrottlesForNavigation adds
domicile::BrowserPageThrottle, which cancels a guest's navigation to
every such page. Canceled rather than blocked: an error page committed
for a WebUI address in a guest is a fatal check of its own. A throttle
rather than a check where
`src` is set, because a link, a redirect and an extension's tabs.update
reach a guest without passing through `src`. Subresources are not
navigations, so the PDF viewer's chrome://resources still loads.

The throttle is //components/domicile:browser_page_throttle, a new
target under src/, added to //chrome/browser:core's deps.

WRITTEN BY HAND, AGAINST THE SERIES RATHER THAN IN A CHECKOUT: the file
each hunk applies to was rebuilt from the pin and the patches before it,
and both blobs are that file's.
---
 chrome/browser/BUILD.gn                                   | 5 +++++
 .../chrome_content_browser_client_navigation_throttles.cc | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
index 5f1cbae288..ca572cccd2 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -1144,6 +1144,11 @@ source_set("core") {
     "//components/device_event_log",
     "//components/dom_distiller/content/browser",
     "//components/dom_distiller/content/common/mojom",
+
+    # Domicile's engine fork: no <webview> is given a page Chrome serves
+    # itself. See chrome_content_browser_client_navigation_throttles.cc.
+    "//components/domicile:browser_page_throttle",
+
     "//components/embedder_support",
     "//components/embedder_support:content_settings",
     "//components/embedder_support:user_agent",
diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client_navigation_throttles.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client_navigation_throttles.cc
index a724121ae1..44a91577f7 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client_navigation_throttles.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client_navigation_throttles.cc
@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@
 #include "components/dom_distiller/content/browser/distiller_referrer_throttle.h"
 #include "components/dom_distiller/core/url_constants.h"
 #include "components/dom_distiller/core/url_utils.h"
+#include "components/domicile/browser/browser_page_throttle.h"
 #include "components/error_page/content/browser/net_error_auto_reloader.h"
 #include "components/guest_view/buildflags/buildflags.h"
 #include "components/history/content/browser/visited_link_navigation_throttle.h"
@@ -310,6 +311,13 @@ void CreateAndAddChromeThrottlesForNavigation(
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
   }
 
+  // Domicile's engine fork. No <webview> is given a page Chrome serves itself:
+  // they are Chrome's UI for Chrome's window, a desk has none, and HistoryUI
+  // took the browser down looking up a tab its guest was not in. After the
+  // main frame's MetricsNavigationThrottle, which has to run before anything
+  // that may cancel.
+  domicile::BrowserPageThrottle::MaybeCreateAndAdd(registry);
+
   DSEPrewarmNavigationThrottle::MaybeCreateAndAdd(registry);
   if (!features::IsDsePreload2Enabled()) {
     SearchPrefetchNavigationThrottle::MaybeCreateAndAdd(registry);
